        "procedure": "To a stirred suspension of ytterbium tri-isopropoxide (1.00 g, 2.86 mmol, used as purchased from Strem at 99.9% purity) in toluene (30 mL) at 25 °C was added a solution of trimethylaluminum (0.617 g, 8.57 mmol) in toluene (30 mL). The mixture was refluxed for 4 h, producing a yellow solution. After filtration and concentration, yellow crystals of 1 were grown at 25 °C (0.41 g, 42%).",
